<Giovanni_Pico_della_Mirandola> <base.kwebbase.kwtopic.has_sentences> "By 1486 Pico had become one of the first Renaissance scholars determined to master Hebrew, which he considered (alongside Latin and Greek) one of the three historic languages of the West, and he realized would give him access not only to the Old Testament in the original, but also to post-biblical Jewish and rabbinic literature - especially the Spanish Cabbalists (like the13th-century visionary Abulafia and the 14th-century Spanish-Jewish philosopher Crescas.) Pico left Florence in May 1486 for Rome, but his journey was interrupted at Arezzo by a scandalous episode when he attempted to elope with the wife of a Medici." .
